==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|ine-pro|*sinos}}; akin to {{cog|sq|gji}} ‘breast, bosom’.<ref>Michiel de Vaan, ''Etymological Dictionary of Latin and the Other Italic Languages'' (Leiden: Brill, 2008), 567.</ref>

The mathematical sense ‘chord of an arc, sine’ was introduced in the 12th century by {{w|Gherardo of Cremona}} as a {{semantic loan|la|ar|جَيْب||chord, sine|nocap=1}} (ultimately a loan from {{der|la|sa|ज्या||bowstring}}) by confusion with {{m|ar|جَيْب||bosom, fold in a garment}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|sinus}}

====Noun====
{{la-noun|sinus<4>}} {{topics|la|Landforms}}

# a [[hollow]], [[cavity]]
# [[curve]], [[fold]], [[winding]]
# [[gulf]], [[bay]]
# [[bosom]]
# [[fold]] of the [[toga]] over the breast, [[pocket]], [[lap]]
# [[heart]], secret [[feelings]]
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin|mathematics}} [[chord]] of an arc, [[sine]]
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} [[fjord]]

